SYNTHESIS
  The decorrelated two-far boundary currency is floor-safe for every bounded core scanned.
  Actual tight rows spend that boundary margin through negative actual-boundary deviation.
  The worst audited rows all have low relation distance far pairs, usually consecutive or near-consecutive.
  Next proof target: boundary currency margin minus signed two-far deviation.

